# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise check
# these files out with CRLF. Two things break when that happens:
#
#  * `scripts/*.sh` — a shell script with CRLF fails in subtle ways (the trailing \r ends up
#    part of the last token on every line), both in CI on Linux and in Git Bash on Windows.
#  * `*.md` — `scripts/okf-docs.sh check` diffs the committed `index.md` files against what
#    `okf index` regenerates, and okf emits LF. With CRLF on disk that diff is never clean,
#    so the gate would be permanently red for a Windows developer after a fresh clone while
#    passing in CI. Pinning LF keeps the gate meaningful on both.
#
# .ps1 files are deliberately left to the default: they are Windows-only by design and
# nothing compares them byte-for-byte.

*.sh  text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
